From 711a639ce6d9cd3010a1e58dc4c8505689a49ab8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 22:10:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Mean thermodynamic forces: weights of the integration points
 cached

computeMeanThermodynamicForcesValues computed, at each call and on the
host, the element transformation of every integration point of the mesh.
On a GPU process, which holds many elements (823,000 for a polycrystal of
6,400 grains on 64 MI300A), this took 2 to 3 s per call: the polycrystal of
mm-opera-hpc calls it after each resolution and at each post-processing,
about 30 % of its wall clock time on the GPUs.

The weights of the points of each behaviour integrator
(getIntegrationPointWeight) are now computed at the first call and kept by
the problem (NonLinearEvolutionProblemImplementationBase::
getIntegrationPointsWeights; the mesh must not be modified afterwards).
The mean values are then sums of the weighted values, material by material,
in the order of the points of each material, which is the order of its
elements: the sums are the same, in the same order (identical outputs of
the polycrystal on the CPU).
